Relation Between the General and the Particular: Entailment vs.\n969:Chalmers, D. (2002a). ‘Consciousness and Its Place in Nature,’ in his Philosophy of Mind:\n983:Correia, F. (2005). Existential Dependence and Cognate Notions. München: Philosophia.\n986:Dancy, J. (2004). Ethics Without Principles. Oxford: Clarendon Press.\n995:Fine, K. (2005). ‘Necessity and Non-Existence,’ in his Modality and Tense: Philosophical\n1003:Levine, J. (2001). Purple Haze. Oxford: Oxford University Press.\n1009:McGinn, C. (1993). Problems in Philosophy. Oxford: Wiley-Blackwell.\n1010:Moore, G. E. (1903/1993). Principia Ethica, 2nd Edition. Cambridge: Cambridge University\n1016:Rosen, G. (2010). ‘Metaphysical Dependence: Grounding and Reduction,’ in R. Hale and\n1024:Schnieder, B. (2006b). ‘A Certain Kind of Trinity: Dependence, Substance, and Explana-\n1026:Sider, T. (2001). Four-Dimensionalism. Oxford: Oxford University Press.\n1027:Skiles, A. (2012). ‘Getting Grounded: Essays on the Metaphysics of Fundamentality’. PhD\n1031:Stoljar, D. (2006). Ignorance and Imagination. Oxford: Oxford University Press.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
